/* TC002CLI/main.swift — hilfetext */
"cli.hilfe" = "mqtttc002 — send messages to an Ulanzi TC002.\n\nUses the setup of the Pixel Clock Messenger app: broker, password and clocks\nare read from there. Setting up happens in the app only.\n\nEvery clock is served on the way that is set for it in the app — HTTP or\nMQTT. \"mqtttc002 clocks\" shows which one.\n\nUSAGE\n  mqtttc002 [send] <text>          send text to the clocks\n  mqtttc002 delete <display>       remove a named display\n  mqtttc002 switch <display>       switch to a display\n  mqtttc002 image <name>           send a finished image from the stock\n  mqtttc002 clocks                 list the clocks that are set up\n  mqtttc002 icons                  list the icons that are there\n  mqtttc002 images                 list the 16x52 images that are there\n  mqtttc002 help                   this text\n\nAn image is a whole display (16x52) from the app's editor and replaces text\nand icon. Of the options below only --to, --name and --duration apply to it;\neverything else formats text, which an image has none of. An AWTRIX NG will\nnot take such an image — its display is 32x8.\n\nOPTIONS FOR \"send\"\n  --to <clock>        name or address; may be given more than once.\n                      Without it, the selection that applies in the app.\n  --name <display>    name of the display on the clock (default: cli)\n  --color #RRGGBB     default: #00FF66\n  --icon <number>     an 8x8 icon to the left of the text\n  --font <name>       default: Silkscreen\n  --size <number>     default: 8\n  --bold              bold cut, if the font has one\n  --upper             everything in capitals\n  --top|--middle|--bottom       vertical alignment (default: middle)\n  --left|--center|--right       horizontal alignment (default: left)\n  --margin <number>   rows left free at top/bottom (default: 1)\n  --gap <number>      empty columns between the characters (default: 1)\n  --duration <seconds>  how long the clock shows the display\n  --speed langsam|mittel|schnell   only for scrolling text\n  --device-font       use the clock's built-in font instead of\n                      rasterizing here. Knows no umlauts.\n  --dry-run           only show what would be sent\n\nThe German names work as well: senden, loeschen, umschalten, bild, uhren,\nbilder, hilfe, --an, --farbe, --schrift, --groesse, --fett, --gross, --oben,\n--mitte, --unten, --links, --zentriert, --rechts, --rand, --abstand,\n--dauer, --tempo, --geraeteschrift, --trocken.\n\nEXAMPLES\n  mqtttc002 \"Coffee ready\"\n  mqtttc002 send \"Mail is here\" --icon 1673 --color \"#FFAA00\"\n  mqtttc002 send Attention --to Kitchen --duration 10 --center\n  mqtttc002 image Heart --name meldung3\n  mqtttc002 delete cli\n\nTexts that are too long scroll by themselves; the app does the same.";

